# File safety & autonomy (Section 3A)

## Workspace

- Build only under `ntn-roaming-lab/` (this repo).
- Reference trees (`URRANSIM_Open5gs`, `3GPP_RAG_SA_LAB`, `5g-ntn-emulation-lab*`, `~/reference/`) are **READ-ONLY**.

## Forbidden on reference trees

- Edit, patch, lint, delete, move, rename
- Git write (`commit`, `checkout`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `pull`, `rebase`)
- Build/install that writes artifacts into reference
- `docker compose up` from a compose file under reference
- Create new files under reference

## Allowed on reference trees

- Read files; copy out into the lab and modify copies
- Read-only git (`log`, `show`, `diff`, `status`, `describe`)
- Record commits in `versions.lock`

## Provenance header on copied files

```
# SOURCE: <reference-path> @ <commit>
# COPIED: <date> — modified for <reason>. Original untouched.
```

## Autonomy

Inside this lab: create/edit/delete, venv installs, Docker, commits — without asking per action.
Continue phases after changelog/commit/tag; batch questions at phase end.

## Autonomy does NOT allow

1. Writes outside this lab (especially reference)
2. Inventing unverifiable spec values (use UNVERIFIED + keep going)
3. Guessing user-only context (ask once, batched)
4. Destructive ops (`docker system prune`, force-push, `rm -rf` beyond build dirs you created) without asking; **never** delete reference/quarantine
